{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And his eyes were dim.</b> From the smoke of these [the sacrifices of Abraham and Isaac]. Another interpretation: when he was bound atop the altar and his father wanted to slaughter him — at that moment the heavens opened and the ministering angels were seen and they wept, and their tears came down and fell upon his eyes; therefore his eyes grew dim. Another interpretation: so that Jacob would take the blessings."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:42.379285371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}